<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $600 mln in Nov 11 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $600 mln in Nov 11 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $600 million in the November 11 week to $3,790.1 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $300 million to $4,838.7 billion. M-1 fell $13.3 billion to $1,067.3 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,784.3 billion versus $3,778.8 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
